  "evaluation": "All three correctly classify the disagreement as genuine, with outcome_measure as the primary reason and population as an additional difference. CES-D symptom presence versus lifetime MDD diagnosis differs in definition and timing within the normalized depression outcome; neither study supplies evidence that its null result was underpowered. A provides the clearest, focused explanation. C is similarly accurate but less descriptive. B is substantively equivalent, though its reference to a general adult population adds an age characterization not explicitly supplied.",
